  "problem_context": {
    "problem_statement": "Reverify CircularAreaWrite and its local callees against the single canonical CircularAreaBackingResource/CircularAreaLogicalState using option-valued mixed_full; make the public contract composable from CircularAreaInit and into CircularAreaRead without assuming uninitialized bytes are initialized.",
    "target_function": "CircularAreaWrite",
    "expected_behavior": "For force=0, preserve error states and append exactly the actually written input prefix to the logical FIFO while updating one or two physical mixed slices and preserving all other cells. Model the production status bit as an equal-index full/empty discriminator. For force!=0, specify only behavior justified by the actual implementation and physical initialization state; do not claim unread initialized bytes that are absent.",
    "input_output_contract": "All real CRTOS call sites use force=0 and must be able to call Write on the resource returned by Init; EOK=0 and ERROR=1. Successful output must establish the same canonical resource consumed by Read/DataLength/Release.",
    "spec_hint": [
      "Use direct Require Export of QCIPLib.xizi.xizi_circular_area_common.xizi_circular_area_lib; define extensional logical/physical ring-update relations in the case lib rather than mirroring C control flow."
